Actually, I agree.  If you had to do all the aligned quests, the game 
designers would have too strongly imposed a single way of achieving one 
goal.  But you *have* to get only two out of three...

Still that may be too few options, especially since the chaotic quest is 
one that normally you can do only after having built up your character 
by far more than what he is when he arrives at that level.  Also, doing 
the chaotic quest in a "reasonable" way more or less forces you to 
genocide lichs (I have done it once without, but I am not eager to 
repeat the experience), which again is restricting your options a bit 
too much.

So you are essentially restricted to neutral plus lawful which leaves 
you with a single way to enter Vlad's tower or you either have to 
genocide lichs or else accept a relatively big risk (if you do it only 
after Gehennom, it may not be that big anymore).
